sion":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Have the drift assertion also verify the installed Pandoc binary's SHA-256 matches the fixture fingerprint (or otherwise justify why version-string equality is sufficient to guarantee identical output bytes), so stale golden bytes cannot pass silently.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4167,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'a fast installed-version drift assertion'","AC: 'A fast assertion fails when the installed Pandoc version differs from fixture metadata.'","Fixture also records 'SHA-256 binary fingerprint' — recorded but not used by the drift assertion","wiki_render.py spawns real pandoc; output bytes are binary-build-dependent, not just version-string-dependent"],"finding":"The drift guard is specified as a version-only assertion ('fast installed-version drift assertion' / 'fails when the installed Pandoc version differs from fixture metadata'), but the golden bytes depend on the actual binary output, which is why the fixture also records a SHA-256 binary fingerprint. Two Pandoc builds sharing a version string but producing different output would pass the version check while the golden bytes are stale, silently weakening the independent oracle.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcd2a5f44beff7d82","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan bullet 2 / AC line 'A fast assertion fails when the installed Pandoc version differs from fixture metadata.'","norm_id":"naea6086ab39e03ee","priority":0.1833,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Local/CI Pandoc pinned to same version string but a rebuilt or patched binary emits different jira output; version check passes, golden comparison silently validates against stale bytes"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Extend the drift assertion to compare the installed binary's SHA-256 against the recorded fingerprint in addition to the version string.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify concretely what strengthening the oracle means (e.g., assert production `_convert` output is byte-identical to the fixture entry for every prepared unit, failing on the first mismatch).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T6","T7","T9"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4625,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Strengthen the oracle so a production format mutation fails against the independent expected output'","No definition of the strengthening beyond the existing byte-equivalence comparison"],"finding":"The plan step 'Strengthen the oracle so a production format mutation fails against the independent expected output' does not specify what 'strengthen' concretely entails beyond replacing the subprocess call with a fixture lookup and byte-comparison — leaving the executor to infer the assertion mechanism.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdc2be63136c84aa6","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan bullet 4 / AC line 'Mutating production output format to plain makes the independent byte-equivalence oracle RED.'","norm_id":"n051ba2510c51e98d","priority":0.1375,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor implements only a lookup+equality check and is unsure whether additional per-unit assertions are required"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State that the oracle asserts each production `_convert` byte output equals the immutable fixture entry keyed by prepared-unit id, and fails the test on any mismatch.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod